The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (call->out_dir_scb != call->out_scb) {
    ret = xdr_decode_AFSFetchStatus(&bp, call, call->out_scb);
}
```
Reason:
This conditional check only decodes the second file status when the source and destination directories are different. If they are the same, the second status is not decoded, causing the xdr pointer to remain unchanged. This results in the volsync record being read incorrectly, leading to potential stale or incorrect status information being used for directory data version updates.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
ret = xdr_decode_AFSFetchStatus(&bp, call, call->out_scb);
if (ret < 0)
    return ret;
```
Reason:
By always decoding the second status regardless of whether the source and destination directories are the same, the xdr pointer is correctly advanced. This ensures that the volsync record is read accurately, allowing the directory data version updates to reference the correct status information, thus fixing the bug.

